	(text "D21 is the only protection part on VOUT: a unidirectional suppressor, 15 V stand-off.\nIt takes electrostatic discharge and, forward biased, the current of the DUT cable when\nthe switch opens on a fault: up to 11.6 A (simulated), rated 50 A for 8.3 ms (datasheet).\nIts leakage adds to the reading: 1 nA typical, 0.1 uA maximum at 15 V, 25 C (datasheet)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 157.48 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "30851d51-9541-5fec-8cdb-b8cd6498991d")
	)
	(text "Nothing resistive hangs on the node after the shunts: its current would be read as\nDUT current. C71 is the only capacitor there (C0G, 100 nF).\nLeakage here and on VOUT adds to the reading: 4 nA to 6 nA typical at 5 V and 40 C\n(estimate). The calibration takes it out with the switch closed and the terminals\nopen; production limit 50 nA at 5.0 V and room temperature."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4065140f-3d80-5ebd-a903-107cab707803")
	)
	(text "U25 copies the node after the shunts.\nVOUT_BUF, behind R119: guard ring around the sense nodes and input of the output\nmonitor. The monitor divider draws 22.7 uA at 5 V: 1.1 mV across R119 (calculated).\nVCCB_SRC, behind R118: supply of the level translator. Two Schottky diodes on the\nDigital Inputs sheet clamp it to ground and +5V: -0.40 V (simulated) to +6.0 V\n(calculated) with U25 at its rails; the limits of the translator are -0.5 V and\n6.5 V (datasheet)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 142.24 52.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8282860e-b3a4-5c8b-9373-3eb59d2fa07e")
	)
	(text "Turn-on: the driver charges C74 and the gates through R117: 2.2 Mohm x 14.2 nF = 31 ms\n(calculated, C74 plus the two gates). Q15 works as a source follower, so VOUT rises\nwith the gate voltage: 90 % of 5 V after about 20 ms, in-rush 0.39 A into 1000 uF and\n0.85 A into 2200 uF (simulated), below the trip level of 1.15 A.\nTurn-off: D20 and R116 discharge the gates into the driver: below 2 V within 7 us\n(simulated). Below one diode drop the gates decay through R117 with 31 ms.\nD20 also clamps the gates a diode drop below ground. R120 damps them while Q15 follows."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 148.844 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9477cbbc-09a9-5e97-8546-eb315596bf10")
	)
	(text "J3 (pin header) and J4 (lever terminal block) carry the same nets, pin 1 to pin 4\nin the order of the PPK2: GND, VIN, VOUT, GND. VIN is the external supply of ampere mode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 157.48 153.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ba421c2a-0993-5fad-85a7-5124da935595")
	)
	(text "R115 holds the gates low through R117 while the driver has no supply. No resistor from\nOUT_GATE or the gate pins to GND or to the sources: with R117 it would divide the gate\nvoltage (100 kohm there leaves 0.52 V, calculated). OUT_GATE is a 2.2 Mohm node: a\n10 Mohm probe lowers the gate from 12 V to 9.8 V (calculated).\nThe firmware closes this switch last and opens it first. For 250 ms after turn-on the\nreading is low by the gate charging current: 0.5 uA at 30 ms, 4 nA at 200 ms (simulated).\nA reading with the switch open is taken 200 ms or more after turn-off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 166.624 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d3eddb68-3b3b-56aa-bda6-34bce0337fe1")
	)
	(text "Instrument off: D21 holds the terminal between about -1 V (estimate) and +16.7 V, its\nlowest breakdown voltage (datasheet); Q16 blocks 30 V (datasheet).\nOutput on: no part bounds VOUT between the set voltage and 16.7 V. No reverse-polarity\nprotection: a source limited to 0.5 A is held near -0.8 V (simulated), a stiff one\ndestroys D21."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 157.48 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eb51cf70-64f4-5b70-8751-5860db063d5c")
	)
